1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,210
A Real Stewart

2
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:03,674
Thanks, Michelle.

3
00:00:03,674 --> 00:00:14,890
I hope you like it.

4
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:17,868
Isn't this baby outfit adorable?

5
00:00:17,868 --> 00:00:21,678
With his name on it--"Max."

6
00:00:21,678 --> 00:00:23,676
Thanks so much, Harry and Michelle.

7
00:00:23,676 --> 00:00:24,640
We really appreciate it.

8
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:25,904
I'm glad you like it.

9
00:00:25,904 --> 00:00:27,071
Michelle picked it out.

10
00:00:27,071 --> 00:00:29,179
Yes, I told Daddy to pick blue ones.

11
00:00:29,179 --> 00:00:32,780
Blue is for boys, and pink is for girls.

12
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:33,758
And Max is some boy.

13
00:00:33,758 --> 00:00:37,236
He's a real Stewart.

14
00:00:37,236 --> 00:00:37,986
Right.

15
00:00:37,986 --> 00:00:40,605
That was so thoughtful of you, Michelle.

16
00:00:40,605 --> 00:00:43,172
Especially to pick it out in blue.

17
00:00:43,172 --> 00:00:47,647
Would you like to see baby Max, Michelle?

18
00:00:47,647 --> 00:00:49,647
Could she? Could we?

19
00:00:49,647 --> 00:00:50,625
Could I?

20
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:52,248
Take them upstairs, Susan.

21
00:00:52,248 --> 00:00:56,270
Harry and Michelle can watch Max sleeping.

22
00:00:56,270 --> 00:00:56,871
Let's go.

23
00:00:56,871 --> 00:00:59,559
Come on, Michelle.

24
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:01,228
Before Max wakes up.

25
00:01:01,228 --> 00:01:08,493
Will you please take this upstairs, Susan?

26
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:09,013
Uh-huh.

27
00:01:09,013 --> 00:01:09,533
Thank you.

28
00:01:09,533 --> 00:01:15,949
Michelle is very grown up for a ten-year-old, huh?

29
00:01:15,949 --> 00:01:18,027
She's smart and sensitive for her age.

30
00:01:18,027 --> 00:01:22,205
Growing up without a mother is difficult.

31
00:01:22,205 --> 00:01:23,749
You mature quickly.

32
00:01:23,749 --> 00:01:25,943
Susan's like a mother to Michelle.

33
00:01:25,943 --> 00:01:29,339
They have a good relationship.

34
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:35,295
Do you think Susan and Harry will get married?

35
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:38,273
Yeah. You can count on it.

36
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:42,083
I think so. Yes. They get along so well.

37
00:01:42,083 --> 00:01:44,229
I like him. He's good for Susan.

38
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:47,630
He's a little quiet.

39
00:01:47,630 --> 00:01:53,734
It's hard to do anything but listen in this family.

40
00:01:53,734 --> 00:01:54,592
You're right, Ellen.

41
00:01:54,592 --> 00:01:56,140
Oh, really?

42
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:59,518
It's the way it should be.

43
00:01:59,518 --> 00:02:01,518
The Stewarts are the Stewarts!

44
00:02:01,518 --> 00:02:02,584
They always were,

45
00:02:02,584 --> 00:02:05,024
and they always will be.

46
00:02:05,024 --> 00:02:05,512
Right!

47
00:02:05,512 --> 00:02:05,874
They've always got an opinion.

48
00:02:05,874 --> 00:02:08,719
Always got something to say.

49
00:02:08,719 --> 00:02:11,405
And now there's Max Stewart.

50
00:02:11,405 --> 00:02:14,848
and if he talks as loudly as he cries,

51
00:02:14,848 --> 00:02:16,868
we're all in for trouble.

52
00:02:16,868 --> 00:02:18,613
He's quiet now.

53
00:02:18,613 --> 00:02:21,304
Mmm-hmm. That's because he's sleeping.

54
00:02:21,304 --> 00:02:32,876
He's really cute.

55
00:02:32,876 --> 00:02:41,079
It's not necessary to whisper, Harry.

56
00:02:41,079 --> 00:02:42,694
A baby gets used to voices.

57
00:02:42,694 --> 00:02:43,501
I remember now.

58
00:02:43,501 --> 00:02:45,424
We always whispered when Michelle was born.

59
00:02:45,424 --> 00:02:47,516
And I didn't sleep well, Daddy told me.

60
00:02:47,516 --> 00:02:48,266
I never slept.

61
00:02:48,266 --> 00:02:49,266
And when I did,

62
00:02:49,266 --> 00:02:52,077
I woke up when I heard someone speak.

63
00:02:52,077 --> 00:02:53,598
I bet you were cute.

64
00:02:53,598 --> 00:02:54,474
She sure was.

65
00:02:54,474 --> 00:02:57,380
Not as cute as Max.

66
00:02:57,380 --> 00:03:11,589
He's like a little doll.

67
00:03:11,589 --> 00:03:12,256
Oh, good.

68
00:03:12,256 --> 00:03:17,402
Now I can help diaper him.

69
00:03:17,402 --> 00:03:18,688
Let's get Marilyn.

70
00:03:18,688 --> 00:03:22,501
What do you do when he cries like that?

71
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:24,901
You pick him up.

72
00:03:24,901 --> 00:03:28,457
He's so little ... so new.

73
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:31,435
Let's call Marilyn.

74
00:03:31,435 --> 00:04:01,215
Time for a feeding and time for a diapering.

75
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:04,215
You're a real Stewart.
